<xml>
  <block type="st_spi_eeprom" x="25" y="25">
    <mutation uid="memory36" />
    <field name="NAME">settings</field>
    <field name="CS">10</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Purpose: Store and read numbers/text in an SPI EEPROM using a separate chip-select.
Hardware: use Connections to check pin ownership for your selected board. Open the comment bubbles on the main steps for explanations.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="25" y="170">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="st_memory_write">
        <field name="DEVICE">memory36</field>
        <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
        <value name="ADDRESS">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">0</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="VALUE">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">1234</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <next>
          <block type="st_memory_text_write">
            <field name="DEVICE">memory36</field>
            <value name="ADDRESS">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">16</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="TEXT">
              <block type="text">
                <field name="TEXT">Hello from EEPROM</field>
              </block>
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="serial_print">
                <value name="CONTENT">
                  <block type="st_memory_read">
                    <field name="DEVICE">memory36</field>
                    <field name="TYPE">uint16_t</field>
                    <value name="ADDRESS">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">0</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="st_memory_text_stream">
                    <field name="DEVICE">memory36</field>
                    <value name="ADDRESS">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">16</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                    <value name="LIMIT">
                      <block type="math_number">
                        <field name="NUM">200</field>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </next>
                <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Send this value/text to the computer. A new line finishes one record; same line can build a record from several values. Match Monitor/Plotter baud to the sketch.</comment>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </next>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="340" h="170">Runs once after power-on or reset. Initialise the program here; repeating measurements and animation belong in loop.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
